# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: cls-hv2
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 6: The Semantics of Classes.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?x, owl:hasValue, ?y)
#   T(?x, owl:onProperty, ?p)
#   T(?u, ?p, ?y)
#     ->  T(?u, rdf:type, ?x)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. No document in this repository asserts owl:hasValue, so
# tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and Python engines on cls-hv2
# zero times and its clean sweep said nothing about it.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to cls-hv2:
#   :x rdf:type :R
#
# The converse of cls-hv1.ttl, and deliberately a separate file: this one starts
# from the PROPERTY assertion and concludes the type, the other starts from the
# type and concludes the property assertion. Putting both in one graph would
# leave each rule's conclusion asserted for the other and neither would fire.
#
# cls-hv1 then fires on the conclusion and re-derives ":x :p :v", which is
# asserted, so it adds no step and takes no credit.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/cls-hv2#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

:R a owl:Restriction ;
   owl:onProperty :p ;
   owl:hasValue :v .

:x :p :v .
